Solid-State Drives (SSDs) Scheduling:
- Linux uses 'none' (noop) or 'mq-deadline' because SSDs have 0 mechanical seek delay.
- Elevating requests by cylinder number on flash storage is unnecessary and adds CPU lock contention.
